   = note: a variant belongs to its enum, so a value names both: `Light.Red`. A bare capitalized
     name is how an error-row tag is spelled, which is why this one did not resolve. In a
     `match` arm the bare name is fine: the scrutinee's type already says which enum.
   = note: `Red` is also a variant of `Card` here; qualify it with the enum you mean.
